David Wang wrote on 24 Nov 2003 12:32:29 GMT in article 
news:<slrnbs3um5.1i6.tjaden@dent.localdomain>:
> [assigning additional intrinsics to improve other DSM]
> 
> On 2003-11-24, Rast <rast2@hotmail.com> wrote:

> > Red dragon scales: Protection and increase damage, +2 in each.  Actual red 
> > dragons should get +4 in each -- they are well known for being the most 
> > fearsome dragons in combat.
> 
> By protection, do you mean it gives additional AC? 

Yeah.  Giving extra points of protection, as if wearing a ring of 
protection, seems to be the easiest way to implement it.

I think even if it was +3 to both damage and AC, it would still be worse 
than SDSM.

> > Orange dragon scales: Free action.
> 
> Orange dragons can be made to breathe paralysis rays for evilness.
> Free action will nullify it, and maybe reflection.

I think sleep is fine, but if the paralysis the duration is really short (1-
2 turns), I don't have a problem with it.

> > Black dragon scales: Level-drain resistance and hallucination resistance. 
> 
> Perhaps give black dragons a drain level bite attack.

Too much like vampires/undead.  

> Why hallucination resistance?

It just seems to fit.
 
> > Blue dragon scales: "Very fast" speed.  (If this turns out to be too strong 
> > an early wish, make it only "fast" speed.)  Boost the speed rating of blue 
> > dragons to 15, from the current 9.
> 
> Intrinsic speed is easily obtained by wand or Quantum Mechanic, so
> just giving it "fast" will not do much.  "Very fast" will make it VERY
> powerful for early wishes though.  How about boosting speed from
> normal to fast and fast to very fast?

That would still be nearly as good as plain old "Very Fast".  Half the 
classes start off as "fast" as it is, and wands of speed monster are rather 
common in my experience.
 
"Very Fast" BlueDSM is a broken early wish, but I'm not convinced it's much 
more broken than GDSM/SDSM or any other early wish is.

"Fast" BlueDSM is useless.  You'll never wish for it, and by the time you 
find a blue dragon, you'll be fast and lightning resistant.
 
> > Yellow dragon scales: Stoning resistance, just like yellow dragons already 
> > have.
> 
> As before, IMHO, stoning resistance is too powerful.

Really?  You'd wear this over SDSM or GDSM on the Planes?

> Stoning is one of the few ways to kill end-game characters, so I'd keep that.

No, its one of the several ways for end-game characters to kill themselves 
stupidly.  If someone has so little confidence in himself that he wants to 
wear this instead of S/GDSM, let him.

> > Let's also reduce the AC bonus of all DSM to 8, rather than 9.  That's still 
> > one more than plate mail/crystal plate mail, which weigh ten times as much.  
> > To partially compensate, change the AC of unenchanted scales from 3 to 4.
> 
> I'd say reducing DSM's base AC to 8 won't do much.  A typical end game
> character has AC between -30 and -40.

Every little bit helps, but my intention here is to make early wishes for 
DSM less powerful.


